### Using JavaScript

You can use JavaScript to manipulate the HTML code before it's rendered into an image. Here’s a basic example using plain JavaScript:

```javascript
function escapeHtml(text) {
    return text.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
}

// Example input
const htmlText = `
<html>
<head>
<title>My Page</title>
</head>
<body>
<p>This is a paragraph with &lt; and &gt; tags.</p>
</body>
</html>
`;

// Escape HTML entities
const escapedHtml = escapeHtml(htmlText);

// Render the HTML content as a string
const renderedHtml = `<img src="data:image/png;base64,${base64.encode(escapedHtml)}" alt="Rendered HTML">`;
```

